# Caddy reverse proxy for the Lightsail host.
#
# Single domain block ONLY — this is deliberate. Caddy's automatic HTTPS
# (docs: A record + ports 80/443 open + domain in config + persistent data
# dir) needs uncontested ownership of the challenge path. A catch-all :80
# reverse-proxy would swallow the ACME HTTP-01 challenge into the app (404)
# and break first issuance, so there is intentionally no :80 block here.
# Direct-IP access is retired: http://<static-ip>/ has no site and 404s;
# use https://semcache.noblechicken.me everywhere (interview links, monitors).
#
# DOMAIN comes from /srv/semcache/app/.env (never committed):
#   DOMAIN=semcache.noblechicken.me
# After any Caddyfile/compose change: `docker compose up -d caddy` (or push —
# the deploy workflow pulls and restarts). Certs issue on first boot after
# DNS propagates and renew forever; watch `docker compose logs caddy` for
# "certificate obtained".

{$DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy app:8000
}
